        "narrative_source": "llm",
        "rationale": "The Committee raised rates by 1/4 percentage point (idx 0) and added language stating that this action will support a timelier return to the 2 percent inflation goal (idx 9), signaling a more assertive stance against inflation. Additionally, the description of inflation was simplified to 'remains elevated' without qualifying supply-shock context (idx 7, idx 8), and productivity/investment language was strengthened to 'strong' and 'robust' (idx 3), reinforcing a more hawkish tone.",
        "summary": "The Federal Reserve raised the target range for the federal funds rate by 1/4 percentage point to 3-3/4 to 4 percent. The statement described economic activity as expanding at a solid pace, with strong productivity growth and robust capital investment. Language citing the conflict in the Middle East as a source of uncertainty was removed, replaced with a reference to geopolitical developments and resilient domestic spending. Inflation was described simply as elevated, without the prior reference to supply shocks in specific sectors like energy. The statement added that the rate increase will support a timelier return to the 2 percent inflation goal. The decision was approved by a vote of 12 in favor with none against.",
        "tone_shift": "more_hawkish"
